  "interpretations": {
    "diag1": "Rule: If the overlap-maximising mode and the nearest-eigenvalue mode coincide with overlap near 1 and all near-zero modes lie in the discrete gradient nullspace, mode misidentification and spurious modes are ruled out.",
    "diag2": "Rule: If the convergence order on the smooth polar quarter-annulus map is about 2, the curvilinear FIT scheme converges at second order on smooth curved walls and the cube-to-disk/ball corner cells are the cause; if not, the scheme itself fails on this geometry.",
    "diag3": "Rule: If corner reconstruction condition numbers grow as a power of N and tangential PEC boundary dual faces S_e have a large normal angle asin(|S_e . n_w| / |S_e|) while corner energy fraction E_loc / E_total shrinks with N, the error comes from boundary dual-face non-orthogonality (fixing d_e = S_e . D = 0 constrains normal D_n) and corner Jacobian degeneration rather than a corner-trapped spurious mode.",
    "diag4": "Rule: If the two-level (4x3x4 -> 8x6x8) definition reproduces the test order and the four-point (N = 6, 8, 12, 16 on NxNxN) definition reproduces the study order, the difference is purely the mesh family and refinement window."
  }
